/-!
# Flat base change for relative dualizing modules

For a flat extension of a Noetherian base ring, the canonical base change map on the
relative dualizing module of a quasi-finite algebra induces an isomorphism after tensoring
with the base-changed algebra.

The mathematics lives in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Different.DualizingModulesQuasi.FlatBaseChange`, which this
module re-exports: `Stacks.Discriminant.dualizingModule_isBaseChange_of_flat`, carrying
`@[stacks 0BT3]`, states that the canonical map exhibits the new dualizing module as scalar
extension of the original one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BT3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BT3)
-/
